import RadiiPolynomial.Certification.IVP.Chebyshev

/-!
# Chebyshev certification adapter — an `L = 2` end-to-end test

A second, materially different data set run through the family faces of
`Certification/IVP/Chebyshev.lean` (`certified_of_checks` and the kernel-scale
`certified_of_checksK`):

| | Example 14.2.1 | this set |
|---|---|---|
| `L` | 1 | 2 |
| `N` | 40 | 6 |
| `ν_q` | 2 | 3/2 |
| `f` | `X₀² − X₀` | `1/10 + X₀X₁`, `−1/10 + X₀²` (cross-coupled) |
| `A`, `DF` off-diagonal | none | nonzero (`A` = exact inverse of `DF(ā)`) |

`ā` is a Newton iterate rounded to `10⁻⁸`; `DF` is the exact block Jacobian at `ā`
(`compPolyDFQ`), `A` its exact rational inverse (so the generated `Z₀` is `0`). Every number is
re-checked by `decide +kernel`. The module is imported by nothing.
-/

